never runs. That is how the first native reading of site 2 came out void -- it reported clean
runs that had driven nothing. The define-held value is what reaches the rule.

What each copy asserts (pop.sh): the run exits 0; QN RETURNED prints, so the drive came back; the
sentinel prints; and at least one PARSERESULT falls between QN BEGIN and QN RETURNED, so the
drive reached parseRule on the NEW road rather than falling back to the old one. The control
copy drives qnAbc, which is green today, and it is what says the template itself works.
